From d04fb3ef68131551b0aadba3fe9ee4cfe38b7f29 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eriko Kurimoto <elkurin@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 23:51:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [Backport] CVE-2026-119266: Use after free in Quota

Cherryy-pick of patch originally reviewed on
https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8603890:
Avoid CopyDirectory fallback in StorageDirectory::DoomPath

Previously, StorageDirectory::DoomPath pre-created a temporary target
directory with base::CreateTemporaryDirInDir and then called
base::Move(path, doomed_dir). When `path` is a symbolic link, moving it
onto an existing directory fails `rename(2)` with EISDIR and falls back
to base::CopyDirectory, which follows the link.

In addition:
- base::PathExists follows symlinks, so a dangling symlink at `path`
  returned early from DoomPath without being removed.
- EnumerateDoomedDirectories and EnumerateDoomedBuckets used
  base::FileEnumerator::DIRECTORIES, skipping doomed symlinks to files
  or nonexistent targets.
- QuotaDatabase::DeleteBucketData returned early on failure without
  clearing doomed bucket directories.

This CL:
- Renames `path` onto a fresh `<name>-doomed-<uuid>` path without
  pre-creating the destination directory, using base::ReplaceFile on
  POSIX (so `rename(2)` does not fall back to CopyDirectory) and
  base::Move (after unlinking reparse points) on non-POSIX platforms,
  and checks base::IsLink so dangling symlinks are also doomed.
- Uses base::FileEnumerator::NAMES_ONLY in EnumerateDoomedDirectories
  and EnumerateDoomedBuckets so any doomed entry is passed to
  base::DeletePathRecursively.
- Calls ClearDoomedBuckets() on early-return error paths in
  QuotaDatabase::DeleteBucketData.

